 Transparent source images are composited onto white for inference so black chemical labels remain visible. The source image is never changed. Table-header inference requires an explicitly marked header row; ordinary first-row data is left for reviewer-supplied headers. Table associations support grouped columns and row spans and allocate IDs across the whole page.
+
+## Book-level acceptance
+
+An 82-page sandbox book was remediated with retained pre-write snapshots: duplicate IDs on 57 pages, 259 link-text edits, reviewed table structure on 12 pages, heading corrections on 15 pages, and 127 reviewed image descriptions. Complex-image descriptions include scientific relationships, data values and units, and chemical or sequence notation where needed. Generated proposals were checked against the actual images and corrected before applying. These content corrections were retained.
+
+A separate controlled alt-text change on an already-remediated page was restored through Conductor. The original long description remained intact; restore rescanned to zero findings and refreshed the matrix. Queue verification remains a reviewer action.
+
+The static scanner has a reproducible jsdom limitation on MathML: even `<math><mi>x</mi></math>` can make axe ARIA checks report a `getComputedStyle` error because the simulated MathML element lacks inline-style support. Related checks remain informational/manual review. Do not suppress these checks or interpret them as a pass; validate mathematical content and rendered-page behavior in a real browser. Keyboard behavior, contrast, and subject-matter adequacy still require reviewer checks.
